{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 4280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, I don't know how widely known this is, but \nmy friend Destin from SmarterEveryDay... he is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8440,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not a fan of teleprompters. Not for himself, and \nhe doesn't like it when other people use them,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11920,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "either. Something about it just isn't as \nauthentic, and you can often see the person's eyes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14840,
    "dDurationMs": 8080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flicking back and forth and back and forth in an \nunnatural way as they read the text. Well, Destin,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some people just aren't as naturally charismatic \nas you are... this video's for the rest of us. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's the thing about teleprompters - those \ntricks of physics where a carefully placed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29000,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "partially transmissive mirror allows you to look \nstraight into the camera lens while simultaneously  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33040,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reading a script off of a screen - if you put one \nclose to you so you can read the text more easily,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then your eyes are visibly moving back and forth \nand it's pretty obvious that you're reading. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40440,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you put it far away, but then it's too small \nto read... There must be some ideal teleprompter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distance and size, right? Yes.\nIt's this equation. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48720,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're getting ahead of ourselves.\nI should also add that I'm definitely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51280,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not an experienced teleprompter user and there \nare plenty of better guides out there for how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to actually perform with a prompter without \nseeming awkward and unnatural - there's more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to it than just getting the distance right. \nBut this video is purely about that - the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61360,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physics of the eye motion and the best distance.\nWhat actually matters for teleprompter eye motion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the experience of the viewer - when they \nare looking at their screen, how much do your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70520,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eyes move in their field of view. Move too much \n(in their perspective) and they might notice. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75200,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The factors that affect the \nteleprompter paradox are these: "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78160,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1) What's the radius of your eyeball? This \ncombined with the rotation of your eyes determines  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how far your irises actually move side to side\n2) How far away are you from the teleprompter?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86600,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Farther away and your eyes will have to \nrotate less to look at the sides of the text "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90000,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3) How wide is the text you're reading? \nThe narrower it is, the less your eyes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94040,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will have to move from side to side\n4) How wide is the camera field of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97520,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "view relative to the motion of your eyes? \nThe wider the view, the smaller your eyes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101080,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will appear and the less (proportionally) your \neyes will move side to side across the screen "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105240,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5) How big is the screen \nthat you're being watched on? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107920,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bigger it is, the bigger your eyes and eye \nmovements will appear to the person watching you "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 6) How far is the viewer from their screen?\nThe farther away they are, the smaller you'll  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116320,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "appear and the harder it'll be for \nthem to notice your eyes moving "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119080,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you combine these six factors together \nusing basic trigonometry, you end up with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122720,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what I'll call the \"teleprompter equation\".\nIt's busy, but not all of it is within your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "control. Like, you can't change the radius of \nyour eye - it's probably about a centimeter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130520,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and will stay that way. And you can't control \nwhat size screen people are using when they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "watch your video, nor how far they sit from \nit. But we can simplify that part anyway,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because people tend to sit closer to little \nscreens and farther from big screens,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145080,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning the ratio of those distances (which \nis in the equation), stays roughly the same. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the question still remains: when your eyes \nmove back and forth, how small should the angle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152800,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they make be from the viewer's perspective?\nHere's where physics really comes into the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "picture: Light is a wave, and waves spread out \nand diffract when they pass through openings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "becoming blurred. So human eyes - with their \npupils - have limits to their resolving power;  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164760,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "typical good human eyes can't distinguish features \nthat are smaller than about a 60th of a degree,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or movements that are about half that \nsize. So if the motion of your eyes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as seen by a viewer, is less than around a \n60th of a degree, they probably won't notice,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176400,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if it's less than a 120th of a degree, \nit's essentially physically impossible for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them to notice. But that's probably overkill.\nSo. We want the \"teleprompter equation\" to be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183880,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at most around a 60th of a degree. Rearranging \nthe equation allows us to come to a conveniently  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simple answer: the distance from the host \nto the screen should be at least 30 times  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the width of the prompter divided by the \nsize of the camera's view, all measured  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195360,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in meters. For feet, it's 100 times the width \nof the prompter divided by the field of view. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, for 30cm wide teleprompter text and \na field of view that's around 2m wide (that is,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204360,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your hands would be just about out of frame),\nthe camera should be at least 4.5m away. Well,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "technically the teleprompter \nshould be 4.5 meters away, so  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the camera will have to be just a touch farther.\nIf you zoom in so the frame is now only 1m wide, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215920,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the teleprompter should be at least 9 \nmeters away! For a small phone teleprompter,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219640,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that same 1 meter frame can have the \ncamera closer - \"only\" 3.6 meters away. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223520,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem, of course, is that it's really \nreally hard to read text on a 12cm phone 3.6  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227800,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meters away. And this is the true essence \nof the teleprompter paradox. In order for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231560,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the viewers to not be able to notice you're \nreading from a teleprompter, the teleprompter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might have to be so far away you can't read it!\nThe only real solutions are to zoom out so the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239320,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "presenter is smaller in the frame (like, \nwith a 2 meter frame it's fine to have a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242560,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phone-sized teleprompter just 1.8 meters away),\nor you need to be ok with sharp-eyed viewers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247080,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being able to notice your eyes moving, or \nyou should use an ear prompter (where the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250640,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "script is read out loud into an earpiece \nin your ear, rather than put on a screen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253880,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you just say out loud what you're hearing).\nIt boils down to this: to avoid detectable eye  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257760,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "motion when using a teleprompter (and therefore \nto avoid judgement by Destin)... Get farther away,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262280,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make your text narrower, or zoom your camera out \n(though zooming out too much can cause the edge of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266560,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the teleprompter to appear in view).\nBut don't get farther away and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269720,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simultaneously make the teleprompter \nbigger... that defeats the purpose."
    } ]
  } ]
}
